{"profile":{"name":"Lily Cheng","ward":"Ward 18, Willowdale","bio":"Lily Cheng was elected to Toronto City Council in October 2022 and took office on November 15, 2022, representing Ward 18 Willowdale, succeeding the retiring John Filion (she had previously run against Filion in 2018). A Willowdale resident for over a dozen years, she is a community organizer who founded North York Moms, co-founded We Love Willowdale after the 2018 Yonge Street van attack, spearheaded the Willowdale Covid Response Network, and served as executive director of the NeighbourLink North York food bank.","committees":["Civic Appointments Committee (Chair)","North York Community Council (Vice-Chair)","Budget Committee","General Government Committee","Toronto Police Services Board","Toronto Police Services Anti-Racism Advisory Panel (Co-Chair)","TO Live Board of Directors"],"contact":{"email":"Councillor_Cheng@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-0210"},"promises":[{"text":"Fight for a Cummer subway station at Yonge and Cummer to serve Willowdale residents, a promise she made in her campaign platform.","source":"https://www.lilycheng.ca/_files/ugd/a54022_931e06e891b446a1a73f27c0a316c5d7.pdf"},{"text":"Advocate for smaller-scale supportive housing and mixed-income and modular housing, and support the regulation of rooming houses.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Improve the community consultation process so that it considers non-English speaking members of the community and better addresses public safety and the loss of green space.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":390,"term":390,"first":"2022-11-17","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":74,"clients":63,"subjects":143,"methods":{"Meetings":153,"Emails":196,"Phone calls":25,"Written":10,"Other or unreported":6},"top":[{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":143},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Official Plan",